// Lays out paragraph i of the view's document inside a text area width_lu lu wide (page width minus margins), refilling its Lay in place: lines, one stride-6 record per line [lo, hi, y, asc, desc, width] with asc including the extra leading so the baseline is y + asc; pen, the x of every code point and one more for the end of the text; h, the whole height with the space before and after. x is measured from the left edge of the text area and already includes indents, alignment and justification; y from the top of the paragraph. Nothing is allocated.
// By hand at 16 px (ascent 14 px = 896 lu, descent 3 px = 192, B and E 683, a space 285, a Normal paragraph with 512 lu after): "BBBB EEEE" in 3500 lu is two lines of 1088 and 2176 + 512 = 2688 in all. A justified "BBB EEE BBB" in 5000 lu stretches its first line to 5000 by 617 on its one inner space. "BE" with the E at 24 pt (ascent 1856, descent 448) is one line 2304 tall. "BB " in 1400 lu keeps its trailing space out of the width 1366 but not out of the pen, whose last entry is 1651. A 150 percent line is 1632 tall. A paragraph with 240 twips before and 480 after (1024 and 2048 lu) is 1024 + 1088 + 2048 = 4160 tall. An E at 24 pt as a superscript is drawn at 18 px and lifted 33 percent of 2048, 675 lu, so its ascent is 16 * 64 + 675 = 1699 and its descent 4 * 64 - 675, below 0, so 0.
lay_para(View v, int i, int width_lu) {
  Para p = v.doc.body.paras[i];
  lp_clear(p.lay.lines);
  lp_clear(p.lay.pen);
} chain (View v, int i, int width_lu) {
  p.lay.h = lp_space(v, i, (import word_p_before));
  lp_lines(v, i, width_lu);
  p.lay.h = p.lay.h + lp_space(v, i, (import word_p_after));
} return void;
